<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Heaven on track to meet yr shr forecast.</title>
<headline>Heaven on track to meet yr shr forecast.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31 vs prospectus forecast for twelve months ending February 28 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>				  1996		  1997 (*)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     4.47	  vs    8.63</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.16	  vs    4.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.67	  vs    6.25</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.51	  vs    2.08</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.43	  vs    1.14</p>
<p>    Turnover		 11.13	  vs   22.03</p>
<p>Full name: Sweets from Heaven Holdings Ltd (food)</p>
<p>NOTE - As the company was only listed on June 12, no comparative figures for the preceding year were provided.</p>
<p>At the time of listing, the company said a maiden dividend, forecast at 2.9 cents a share, would be payable in June next year. The company said it was confident that, based on current conditions, prospectus forecasts would at least be met.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
